  "body": "The HTML document below displays a `<canvas>` tag in an `<iframe>`. The `<canvas>` tag has a red dot as background image provided as a data URI.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n\r\n<body>\r\n    <iframe srcdoc=\"\r\n        <!DOCTYPE html> \r\n        <html>\r\n            <body>\r\n                <canvas style='background-image:url(&quot;data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAUAAAAFCAYAAACNbyblAAAAHElEQVQI12P4//8/w38GIAXDIBKE0DHxgljNBAAO9TXL0Y4OHwAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==&quot;)'></canvas>\r\n            </body>\r\n        </html>\">\r\n    </iframe>\r\n</body>\r\n\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI noticed that the size of the canvas is 0x0 if I add the attribute `sandbox` to the `<iframe>` tag. I also noticed that I must set the attribute `sandbox` to `allow-scripts` to fix the issue. These behaviors have been seen in Firefox and Chrome so I suppose this is specified somewhere. Where can I find the documentation specifying this behavior?",
